WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.130
- No matter what you
think of Michael Cohen,

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.843
he can wear a suit coat.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.363
He's got that going
for him, which is nice.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.000
Michael Cohen would make a
great, great movie character.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.690
In fact, his life often seems
more like fiction than fact.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.280
That Cohen could hold
the key to how much legal

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.330
and political trouble his estranged,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.710
one-time, boss Donald Trump
is in, feels somehow fated,

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.730
written in the stars as
though this is the only way

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.360
the story of the The Donald
and Michael could end.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.520
Now that story begins

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.120
in the most New York City way
possible, a condo board fight.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.490
Starting in 2001, Cohen
owned a condominium

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.690
in Trump World Tower,

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.200
a building near the United
Nations in the Big Apple.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.070
Cohen convinced his parents, his in-laws

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.820
and a business partner to also
buy condos in that building.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.830
Cohen got himself on the
condo board at the building

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.740
and, in a fight between Trump
and some of the tenants,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.610
Cohen took Trump's side.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.630
Don't act surprised.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.220
So Trump said, who is this guy?

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.080
My lawyers that I give
thousands of dollars to

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:00.990
couldn't do it.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:01.823
I'd like to meet him.

00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:05.310
Cohen's uncle, Dr. Morton Levine,
told the Associated Press.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.880
So, the two men met.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.350
Cohen, who had read The Art of
The Deal not once but twice,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.430
clearly impressed Trump.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.700
And the rest is history.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.420
Of that moment, Trump
recently told Fox News this.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.440
Years ago, many years,
like 12, 13 years ago,

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.880
he did me a favor.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.620
He was on a committee, and he
was so responsive and so good,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.520
and I said, he's a nice guy.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.260
Now, Trump hired Cohen

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.360
to work as a sort of jack of all trades

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.470
for The Trump Organization,

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.940
but really to work for him, in 2006.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.090
And Cohen has been described
as many things to Trump,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.120
personal lawyer, fixer,
confidante, intimidator,

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.510
and some things I just
can't say even on YouTube.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.620
And here's how Cohen
himself described his job

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.820
in an interview with ABC News in 2011.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.820
Quote, if somebody does
something Mr. Trump doesn't like,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.070
I do everything in my power

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.320
to resolve it to Mr. Trump's benefit.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.680
If you do something wrong,
I'm going to come at you,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.740
grab you by the neck,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.290
and I'm not going to let
you go until I'm finished.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.330
Gee, sounds kind of ominous, right?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.260
That was the point.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.950
Over the decade between 2006 and 2016,

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.750
Cohen repeatedly distinguished himself

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.650
and won Trump's ongoing
loyalty by being willing to say

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.990
and do things for Mr.
Trump, as Cohen relentlessly

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.460
referred to the billionaire,
that no one else would do.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.980
He was the most loyal guy,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.790
the guy who would always
have Trump's back,

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.430
whether on a business deal
for some new golf property,

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.070
or in yelling at a magazine editor

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.070
for not including Donald Trump on a list

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.790
of the 200 most influential New Yorkers,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.000
which of course actually happened.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.410
Now that loyalty paid off
(cash register dings),

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.060
literally, for Cohen.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.470
He shopped his connection to
Trump around wherever he went.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.090
Now, some of it was innocuous,
if sort of pathetic.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.560
One woman told the Washington Post

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.530
that she ran into Cohen at
their kids' baseball game,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.610
and that Cohen whipped out his phone

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.750
to show her pictures of Trump
at his son's bar mitzvah.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.450
Quote, he was very proud,
she told the Post of Cohen.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.630
I'll bet.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:06.680
But Cohen was doing a lot more

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.360
than just showing off his
kid with a famous guy.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.370
Over the decade he worked with Trump,

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.210
he played off his
closest-to the billionaire

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.930
real estate mogul to feather
his own nest repeatedly,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.310
through his law practice
using his work for Trump

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:23.030
as a trump card for perspective clients.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.520
He amassed a fortune in taxi medallions,

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.300
the little medals required
to own a cab in the city.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.840
He invested in an offshore
gambling operation

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.440
near Miami, which failed.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.720
In short, Cohen became
a mini version of Trump,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.560
with the successes and the failures,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.450
a wheeler-dealer who fixed problems

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.780
for a bigger wheeler-dealer.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.730
By the time Trump started
running for president in 2016,

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.380
Cohen was alternately described
as the sixth Trump child,

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.900
Trump's Tom Hagen, it's
a Godfather reference

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.140
for those of you under 30,

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.460
or Trump's Michael Clayton,
a deeply underrated movie.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.960
Then, it all went wrong as
it always, always goes wrong.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.150
I told you, this was like
a particularly juicy novel.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.020
In the course of the 2016 campaign,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.960
Cohen orchestrated hush
money payments to two women,

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.140
porn star, Stormy Daniels,

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.890
and Playboy model, Karen McDougal,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.900
who alleged they had affairs with Trump

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.890
during the mid-2000s.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.060
Trump denies those affairs.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.170
Now, questioned about
the source of the money

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.520
for the six-figure payment to Daniels

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.160
in exchange for her silence, Cohen lied,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.700
said it was his own money

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.840
and that Trump never knew
anything about any payments.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.360
Now that was just one of the many lies

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.780
Cohen now admits to telling.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.250
Another biggie, how about
when he told Congress

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.150
he had cut off all
conversations with the Russians

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.450
about a Trump Tower Moscow development

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:42.520
way back in January, 2016.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.800
Turns out, as Cohen later admitted,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.747
those conversations were
ongoing through June, 2016.

00:04:48.747 --> 00:04:50.870
Now Cohen said he lied about the timing

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.930
of the Russian conversations
because he was worried

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.380
telling the truth might
hurt Trump's chances

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.940
of winning the White House.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.100
Now everything changes for Cohen and Trump

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.340
on April 9, 2018.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.740
That's the day the FBI raids Cohen's home,

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.020
office and hotel room.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.450
Sidebar, what normal person has a house

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.140
and a hotel room in the same city?

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.610
Hunh, the feds seized
thousands of documents,

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.110
emails and other notes on Cohen's
various business dealings,

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.460
both for Trump and for
himself, in that raid.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.320
Now, Cohen initially
denied any wrongdoing.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:27.410
Trump called the raid, quote,
an attack on our country.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.980
But it slowly but surely became clear

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:33.890
that Cohen's long-time,
unflinching loyalty to Trump

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.850
was eroding badly.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.360
By late August, 2018, he had cut a deal,

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.060
pleading guilty on eight criminal counts

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.310
and agreed to cooperate
with the ongoing probe

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.890
surrounding Trump's 2016 campaign.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.640
And Cohen also dropped this bombshell.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.890
He said he coordinated the
payments to Daniels and McDougal

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.270
at the direction of Trump who, Cohen said,

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.810
coordinated the whole thing,

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.620
which made the President
of the United States,

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.680
in Cohen's version of events at least,

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.880
an unindicted coconspirator

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.900
in a plot to end-run campaign
finance law to preserve

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.920
and better his chances of
winning the White House.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:10.800
Yeah.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.500
Trump denies everything, of course.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.820
- Michael Cohen is lying,

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.040
and he's trying to get a reduced sentence

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.030
for things that have
nothing to do with me.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.260
- Quote, I never directed
Michael Cohen to break the law.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.450
He was a lawyer, and he is
supposed to know the law,

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.370
Trump tweeted in December, 2018.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:28.420
And, Trump later told Fox
News that the prosecutors,

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.420
quote, put those two charges
on to embarrass me, end quote.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.860
But, before Cohen heads to jail in May

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.280
to serve a three-year
sentence for his crimes,

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.910
he'll get a chance to
tell his story to Congress

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.570
and the public, who will
most definitely be watching.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.520
For a man who famously
pledged he'd take a bullet

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.780
for Trump, Michael Cohen
could now be the one

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:56.780
who bangs a final nail into
Trump's political coffin.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.123
And that is The Po!nt.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.830
We make episodes twice a week,
so make sure to check back

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.823
every Tuesday and Thursday for
brand new political content.

